{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2928fab7759433a4cf13333b8314528515f69ccc28bf9ba07db36fda082db478"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tutorial project 'Mya Ri Store' is a buyer flow: product list, cart, checkout form (name/phone/address), order summary, then sending a screenshot to the seller via Viber."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2f18a496d3eb97a131a2c0662c6f7592ce4ad692b3c807ad97e401c98573c2c3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tutorial project is built with React, Vite, and Tailwind CSS, and is designed to run without a backend or rented server."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3c73358b899a5e1ea0f25aa8e8224da5d5a60523008c216eaa4196b1d5a05cf2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Readers need a computer (macOS/Windows/Linux), Claude Code with a Pro/Max/Team/Enterprise plan or Console account, Node.js v18 or later, and basic Git knowledge."},{"claim_ids":["clm_448a0f949b88114c5c148a342bbae10c5976fcaf6c01c6b0c4ca647435318908"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The book has nine chapters in markdown files under chapters/, covering topics from what agentic coding is, to Claude Code setup, instructing agents, skills, and context/token economy."},{"claim_ids":["clm_44f896373e747c4873f6fe377b2be43a8334bd89a0ac492dab2c1a458bc0efc1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Building the book requires python3 and a Chromium-based browser for PDF generation, with an optional CHROME environment variable pointing to the browser path."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5292c039a5207c5dcf1fdb723ce95fd3be4b5c0f15b1f89605a30fca2d005d08"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"On first run, build.sh creates a Python venv at build/venv, installs markdown and fonttools, embeds the Noto Sans Myanmar font, and assembles chapters into EPUB/PDF."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6a6ca2e2bb999fc5f0ed52acb8a07b427c43f753c5e3441aa6e4b21c5266987e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The build script targets macOS by default because it uses the system-installed Noto Sans Myanmar font; on other OSes the regular and bold TTF files must be placed manually in build/."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6b2fd738bc4fe0a75f7db723938903c93e8fd3f1120e34204594f1db4993f167"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The book is positioned as a lightweight bootstrap for beginners, not a path to full mastery, and points to the author's PitWay project for deeper engineering-workflow topics."},{"claim_ids":["clm_70fd6c687dbf13f388a44c2d20160d58218c653d6112e6a15190bcc184941e13"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository is a Burmese-language tutorial book on agentic coding with Claude Code, aimed at junior/noob developers, using a mini ecommerce project as its running example."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a6f9f818e3822c35cd4bc35d4e5f19dfc582fdb69aa3f6ce65364a21a0f0cfa8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Chapter 3 teaches instructing agents via CLAUDE.md, Plan Mode, and prompt-writing style."},{"claim_ids":["clm_af090a3be29dd645e65694cb1f780a5ad10ed32e494ac51d519106edee0221cb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The repository is MIT licensed (Copyright 2026 Soe Thura), while the embedded Noto Sans Myanmar font is under the SIL Open Font License."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d5d7beab0b47387ca94e676d5741acf677f94281b5194d07964cd9a227923065"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Chapter 7 covers building reusable Skills, including SKILL.md structure and three ways to reuse them."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ee1b3433bfd2e77a5ceae912a79c1e6153fd320c9fc3336abd6c5c90b24175f3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A build.sh script at the repo root produces EPUB and PDF outputs (both, or either alone) into dist/, with named files agentic-coding-basic-mm.epub and .pdf."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2928fab7759433a4cf13333b8314528515f69ccc28bf9ba07db36fda082db478","clm_2f18a496d3eb97a131a2c0662c6f7592ce4ad692b3c807ad97e401c98573c2c3","clm_3c73358b899a5e1ea0f25aa8e8224da5d5a60523008c216eaa4196b1d5a05cf2","clm_448a0f949b88114c5c148a342bbae10c5976fcaf6c01c6b0c4ca647435318908","clm_44f896373e747c4873f6fe377b2be43a8334bd89a0ac492dab2c1a458bc0efc1","clm_5292c039a5207c5dcf1fdb723ce95fd